   "html_text": "The conservation biology framing interprets “biodiversity” as a term that is to capture everything we want to conserve. An emerging socio-ecological framing of biodiversity requires that the term take on a broader scope—it is to be made operational, not just for conservation, but more broadly for sustainability, encompassing the many ways that society and nature are inter-linked. While conservation biology has interpreted “biodiversity” as, from the start, all about society’s conservation values",
   "md_text": "The conservation biology framing interprets “biodiversity” as a term that is to capture everything we want to conserve. An emerging socio-ecological framing of biodiversity requires that the term take on a broader scope—it is to be made operational, not just for conservation, but more broadly for sustainability, encompassing the many ways that society and nature are inter-linked. While conservation biology has interpreted “biodiversity” as, from the start, all about society’s conservation values"
  },
  {
   "i": 224,
   "shape_h": "ol",
   "shape_m": "ol",
   "html_text": "“biodiversity” as biological (variation), and the benefit of variety as having normative importance, what is conserved as having normative importance, and the meaning of “biodiversity” obliged to capture all that, “biodiversity” as purely biological, and so needing a re-casting to gain normative status.",
   "md_text": "“biodiversity” as biological (variation), and the benefit of variety as having normative importance, what is conserved as having normative importance, and the meaning of “biodiversity” obliged to capture all that, “biodiversity” as purely biological, and so needing a re-casting to gain normative status."
